 ## Subtopics
 
+### [Align Your Gaussians (AYG)](14896-align-your-gaussians-ayg.md)
+A text-to-4D synthesis method that generates dynamic 3D Gaussian Splatting scenes from text prompts. It solves the problem of creating temporally consistent, deformable 3D content by endowing static 3DGS with dynamics via a deformation network. It is distinguished from static 3D generation methods by its explicit modeling of motion through a text-to-video diffusion prior, and from other 4D methods like DreamGaussian4D by its use of a text-to-video model for motion capture rather than learning motion from a driving video. Choose it when dynamic 4D scene synthesis is required. [Align Your Gaussians (AYG)](14896-align-your-gaussians-ayg.md)
+
+### [Conditional 3D Gaussian Splatting Generation](15578-conditional-3d-gaussian-splatting-generation.md)
+Produces 3D Gaussian Splatting representations directly from text prompts, input images, or partial 3DGS inputs containing large occlusions. It solves the problem of controllable 3D asset creation and scene completion without relying on iterative per-scene optimization or explicit intermediate image sets, amortizing reconstruction cost by learning a feedforward or diffusion-based mapping. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Align Your Gaussians (AYG)](14896-align-your-gaussians-ayg.md) by focusing on static or diffusion-based generation conditioned on semantic or geometric priors rather than dynamic 4D scene synthesis. Choose it for static or diffusion-based generation with semantic/geometric conditioning. [Conditional 3D Gaussian Splatting Generation](15578-conditional-3d-gaussian-splatting-generation.md)
+
 ### Latent Diffusion Model (LDM) for 3DGS
-A diffusion model trained in the latent space of the Gaussian VAE to generate novel 3DGS shapes conditionally or unconditionally [S2]. It differs from direct pixel-space diffusion by operating on the compressed latent representation of the Gaussian functions, enabling efficient generation of diverse 3DGS [S2].
-*   **Training:** The LDM is trained to predict noise or reverse the diffusion process on latent vectors $z_k$ derived from the VAE [S2].
-*   **Generation:** Starts from noise $N(0,1)$, iteratively denoises to $z_0$ (Step K to Step 0), conditioned on text, image, or partial GS if applicable [S2].
+A diffusion model trained in the latent space of the Gaussian VAE to generate novel 3DGS shapes conditionally or unconditionally [S2]. It differs from direct pixel-space diffusion by operating on the compressed latent representation of the Gaussian functions, enabling efficient generation of diverse 3DGS [S2]. Choose it when efficient, latent-space diffusion is preferred for 3DGS generation [S2].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Near-real-time sampling at test time [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing the trained feedforward or diffusion model and the VAE [S1, S2].
-*   **Strengths:** Amortizes reconstruction cost; naturally promotes multi-view coherence; enables near-real-time sampling [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires large, curated 3D training corpora; challenges in maintaining controllability (e.g., disentangling geometry from appearance) while scaling [S1]; imperfect cross-view consistency can lead to noisy geometry in occluded regions [S1].
-*   **When to use:** When rapid generation from text/images is required and iterative optimization is too slow [S1].
-*   **When not to use:** When exact reconstruction of a specific input is required without generative artifacts [S1].
